        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most owners, the right bag is simply the genuine part for your drum: RIDGID's VF3502 for a 12 to 16 gallon RIDGID, Shop-Vac's Type J for a standard large Shop-Vac, DEWALT's DXVA19-4102 for a DXV drum. Buy high efficiency for drywall and sanding, HEPA for concrete and tile dust, and skip the bag entirely for coarse debris and water.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Check the fit once, change the bag on suction rather than volume, and never vacuum ash that is not stone cold. Do that and a pack of bags will save you more in cartridges and cleanup than it costs.
          </p>
